  "officialHtml": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/plc1800.html",
  "prefLabel": "Plc 1808.03 Professional Obligations",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Plc 1808.03 Professional Obligations. Each person subject to this chapter shall:\n\n(a) Comply with RSA 310-C, Plc 300, and Plc 1800;\n\n(b) Comply with any disciplinary or remedial orders issued by the executive director within the time periods specified;\n\n(c) Interact with colleagues and clients with honesty and integrity;\n\n(d) Cooperate with inspections and with lawful investigations by the executive director;\n\n(e) Treat all individuals with whom the person interacts in a professional capacity with respect and civility;\n\n(f) Maintain sexual boundaries by:\n\n(1) Refraining from any behavior that exploits the assessor-client relationship in a sexual way; and\n\n(2) Avoiding any behavior that is sexual or sexually demeaning, or that could be reasonably interpreted as such, even when initiated by or consented to by the client or colleague;\n\n(g) Not engage in hazing or sexual, verbal, or physical harassment of any individual when interacting in a professional capacity; and\n\n(h) Not discriminate based on age, sex, gender identity, race, creed, color, marital status, familial status, physical or mental disability, or national origin.\n\nSource. #14330, eff 9-22-25, EXPIRES: 9-22-35",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/plc1800.html"
}
